{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MountRegistry","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This type exists for safety, not bookkeeping.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" In "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mount(8)"},{"type":"text","text":" output, a mount made"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by grrclone is indistinguishable from one a user made by hand: both appear as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"localhost:\/ on \/Users\/x\/Something (nfs, ... mounted by x)"},{"type":"text","text":". The development machine"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for this project runs exactly such a hand-rolled setup, mounting two remotes via a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"launchd agent."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A reconciler that force-unmounts every "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"localhost:\/"},{"type":"text","text":" NFS mount would therefore"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destroy the user’s own volumes, potentially mid-write. So grrclone unmounts a path"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only if that exact path is recorded here, written before the mount is attempted and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"removed after a successful unmount. Matching on mount source, port, or process name"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is never sufficient evidence of ownership."}]}]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/docs.GrrCloneCore\/documentation\/GrrCloneCore\/MountRegistry\/Entry"],"title":"Structures","anchor":"Structures","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/docs.G